{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463390",
      "title": "How Vue Updates the DOM",
      "lectureOrder": 67,
      "videoOrder": 60,
      "sourceHash": "0be50d27930e61a0af49a5289a8a2d28a65ff9dca32615c33ed8b1b14fdae539",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.8,
          "en": "Now we already learned about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.8,
          "end": 8.57,
          "en": "a couple of nice behind the scenes and core features of Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.57,
          "end": 11.44,
          "en": "Let's now understand how it actually updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.44,
          "end": 13.09,
          "en": "what we see on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.09,
          "end": 16.15,
          "en": "Of course we learned about it's built in reactivity,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.15,
          "end": 19.27,
          "en": "but this is basically just how Vue detects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.27,
          "end": 23.06,
          "en": "that an update is needed and where the update is needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.06,
          "end": 27.48,
          "en": "But performing that update in a performance optimized way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.48,
          "end": 29.54,
          "en": "is yet another thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.54,
          "end": 31.03,
          "en": "And I mentioned this before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.03,
          "end": 33.41,
          "en": "and I'm going to show it to you again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.41,
          "end": 38.41,
          "en": "If I inspect an element here in the browser developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 42.79,
          "en": "you will notice that if I type here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.79,
          "end": 46.28,
          "en": "and I click set text, only the paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.28,
          "end": 49.863,
          "en": "with the text inside of it flashed here on the right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.72,
          "end": 53.95,
          "en": "So Vue only updated this paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.95,
          "end": 56.08,
          "en": "and nothing else on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.08,
          "end": 61.08,
          "en": "And Vue does that with a concept called the virtual DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.82,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "So how does that work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 66.67,
          "en": "And why does view update to DOM like this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.67,
          "end": 69.07,
          "en": "We got our Vue Instance, our view app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.07,
          "end": 71.27,
          "en": "and we got the DOM, the Browser DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.27,
          "end": 74.66,
          "en": "So the HTML content rendered by the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.66,
          "end": 76.22,
          "en": "and therefore essentially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.22,
          "end": 78.473,
          "en": "what the user is able to see on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.65,
          "end": 83,
          "en": "Our Vue app, our Vue Instance, stores data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83,
          "end": 85.08,
          "en": "computed properties, and methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.08,
          "end": 88.06,
          "en": "And the Browser DOM is then influenced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.06,
          "end": 90.64,
          "en": "with help of the view controlled template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.64,
          "end": 93.44,
          "en": "That template content is rendered to the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.44,
          "end": 97.62,
          "en": "And during that rendering process, which Vue controls,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 101.75999999999999,
          "en": "the dynamic parts and placeholders, the interpolations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.75999999999999,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "and bindings, are removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 107.47,
          "en": "and the actual values are inserted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.47,
          "end": 109.97,
          "en": "I mean, that is what you can see here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.97,
          "end": 111.75999999999999,
          "en": "We got the paragraph tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.75999999999999,
          "end": 114.22,
          "en": "with the test text being rendered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.22,
          "end": 116.08,
          "en": "We don't have the curly braces here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.08,
          "end": 119.793,
          "en": "yet we of course do have them here in our template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.74,
          "end": 123.86,
          "en": "On the button, we got this @click thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.86,
          "end": 125.86,
          "en": "which is an instruction to Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.86,
          "end": 127.58,
          "en": "and that's why we don't see it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.58,
          "end": 130.7,
          "en": "in the actual DOM that's rendered in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.7,
          "end": 134.73,
          "en": "Because those Vue instructions are removed by Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.73,
          "end": 138.04,
          "en": "when it renders its template to the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.04,
          "end": 141.01,
          "en": "So when it basically converts its template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.01,
          "end": 143.71,
          "en": "to the actual HTML elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.71,
          "end": 146.03300000000002,
          "en": "that should be shown on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.38,
          "end": 149.21,
          "en": "That's what Vue does here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.21,
          "end": 151.93,
          "en": "And therefore, if we have data like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.93,
          "end": 154.6,
          "en": "we see something like this on the screen instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.6,
          "end": 158.8,
          "en": "if we use interpolation for outputting the data for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.8,
          "end": 160.91,
          "en": "Now of course our data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.91,
          "end": 164.02,
          "en": "and our computed properties might change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.02,
          "end": 166.51,
          "en": "For example, because the user entered something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.51,
          "end": 169.1,
          "en": "or clicked a button and those updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.1,
          "end": 170.84,
          "en": "should of course be reflected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.84,
          "end": 174.07,
          "en": "but Vue should not re-render the entire page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.07,
          "end": 175.92000000000002,
          "en": "every time something changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.92000000000002,
          "end": 178.76,
          "en": "but only the parts that did change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 178.76,
          "end": 181.36,
          "en": "Because if Vue would reevaluate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.36,
          "end": 183.82,
          "en": "and re-render the entire page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.82,
          "end": 186.57,
          "en": "well that would not be great for performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.57,
          "end": 189.47,
          "en": "if just one piece of text changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.47,
          "end": 192.13,
          "en": "For example, if just the title changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.13,
          "end": 194.43,
          "en": "but not the text property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 194.43,
          "end": 197.63,
          "en": "then only the h2 tag, which outputs the title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 197.63,
          "end": 200.203,
          "en": "should be updated and not the paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 201.14,
          "end": 204.19,
          "en": "Now, how could Vue ensure that this is the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.19,
          "end": 207.76,
          "en": "that it does not re-render the entire screen?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.76,
          "end": 210.13,
          "en": "Well, one possible solution would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.13,
          "end": 213.97,
          "en": "that it basically compares the old DOM values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 213.97,
          "end": 215.24,
          "en": "with the new ones.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 215.24,
          "end": 218.87,
          "en": "So it basically goes through the entire rendered DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 218.87,
          "end": 221.15,
          "en": "sees which content is in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.15,
          "end": 224.61,
          "en": "and compares that to the content it has stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 224.61,
          "end": 227.15,
          "en": "in the data properties of the Vue app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 227.15,
          "end": 229.433,
          "en": "And if there's a difference, it updates it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 231,
          "end": 232.77,
          "en": "Well it could do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.77,
          "end": 236.77,
          "en": "And at least it would not update the entire screen then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 236.77,
          "end": 239.32999999999998,
          "en": "but actually it's not what it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 239.32999999999998,
          "end": 243.54,
          "en": "because reading the entire real DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.54,
          "end": 246.44,
          "en": "which is rendered by the browser all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.44,
          "end": 247.98,
          "en": "whenever something changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 247.98,
          "end": 250.61,
          "en": "is also pretty performance intensive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 250.61,
          "end": 254.47,
          "en": "Maybe not as bad as re rendering the entire page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.47,
          "end": 257.82,
          "en": "all the time, but definitely not great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 257.82,
          "end": 260.02,
          "en": "Instead, as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 260.02,
          "end": 264.01,
          "en": "Vue uses a concept called the Virtual DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 264.01,
          "end": 268.58,
          "en": "It basically has a virtual copy of the real DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 268.58,
          "end": 271.74,
          "en": "which is managed entirely in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 271.74,
          "end": 273.423,
          "en": "and therefore in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 274.61,
          "end": 276.15,
          "en": "It could look something like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 276.15,
          "end": 280.5,
          "en": "a bunch of JavaScript objects where Vue memorizes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.5,
          "end": 282.72,
          "en": "which HTML tag is needed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 282.72,
          "end": 285.023,
          "en": "and what the content of that tag is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.49,
          "end": 290.26,
          "en": "And when data changes, it basically just creates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.26,
          "end": 292.6,
          "en": "a new Virtual DOM you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 292.6,
          "end": 297.6,
          "en": "and compares the new Virtual DOM to the old Virtual DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 297.72,
          "end": 302.36,
          "en": "and only differences between those Virtual DOMS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.36,
          "end": 304.71,
          "en": "are written to the real DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 304.71,
          "end": 306.61,
          "en": "And that is way more efficient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306.61,
          "end": 310.93,
          "en": "because doing such comparisons and updates in a Virtual DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 310.93,
          "end": 313.36,
          "en": "and therefore entirely in memory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 313.36,
          "end": 316.83,
          "en": "is way more efficient than doing it in the real DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 316.83,
          "end": 318.653,
          "en": "which was rendered to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 319.86,
          "end": 322.15,
          "en": "And that's how Vue does that behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 322.15,
          "end": 323.6,
          "en": "Whenever we change something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 323.6,
          "end": 325.52,
          "en": "whenever I changed this text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 325.52,
          "end": 329.26,
          "en": "and I click set text, Vue detects this change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 329.26,
          "end": 332.7,
          "en": "thanks to the reactivity we discussed earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 332.7,
          "end": 337.32,
          "en": "in this module, and then it creates a new Virtual DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 337.32,
          "end": 340.34000000000003,
          "en": "compares it to the old Virtual DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 340.34000000000003,
          "end": 344.12,
          "en": "and detects the differences, and then updates the part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 344.12,
          "end": 348.13,
          "en": "in the real DOM where the differences were detected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 348.13,
          "end": 350.8,
          "en": "That is what Vue does in a nutshell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 350.8,
          "end": 353.09000000000003,
          "en": "Now it should be needless to say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 353.09000000000003,
          "end": 356.6,
          "en": "that Vue has a bunch of optimizations in place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 356.6,
          "end": 360.16,
          "en": "that actually make this way more performant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 360.16,
          "end": 362.84,
          "en": "In reality, it does not recreate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 362.84,
          "end": 365.37,
          "en": "entire virtual DOM's all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 365.37,
          "end": 367.85,
          "en": "It has a bunch of optimizations for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 367.85,
          "end": 370.02,
          "en": "but this is beyond the scope of this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 370.02,
          "end": 371.89,
          "en": "And really also not something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 371.89,
          "end": 373.76,
          "en": "you'd need to know necessarily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 373.76,
          "end": 376.74,
          "en": "You should just know how it generally works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 376.74,
          "end": 381,
          "en": "to be aware of what Vue does, that it's not all magic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 381,
          "end": 383.86,
          "en": "but that it's pretty, pretty performant.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
